# Contributing to NLCS CS Tasks

This repository holds the interactive tasks and resources for NLCS Jeju Computer Science (Years 5–14). It is published to students through GitHub Pages, so anything merged into `main` goes live.

## Who can contribute

Members of the **CS-Staff** team have write access. If you need access, ask a member of **CS-Admins** to invite your GitHub account to the organization.

## How to add a new task

1. **Create a branch.** Don't commit to `main` directly (it is protected). Name the branch after the task, for example `add-yr8-binary-quiz`.
2. **Add your HTML file** to the repository root. Use a clear file name with no spaces, e.g. `Yr8_Binary_Quiz.html`. File names are case-sensitive on GitHub Pages.
3. **Keep it self-contained.** Put CSS and JavaScript inside the HTML file where you can. If you need images, put them in an `assets/` folder and link to them with relative paths.
4. **Add a card to `index.html`.** Copy an existing card inside `<div class="grid">` and change:
   - the comment (`<!-- Card N: Title -->`)
   - `data-tags`: lowercase search keywords (year group, topic, syllabus code)
   - the title and a one-sentence description
   - two or three tags (e.g. `Year 8`, `Binary`, or a syllabus code such as `A3.4.3`)
   - the `href`, which must match your file name exactly (`./Yr8_Binary_Quiz.html`)
5. **Open a pull request** into `main`. A CS-Admin will review it and merge it, and the page updates on the live site within a few minutes.

## Card template

```html
<!-- Card N: Task Title -->
<div class="card" data-tags="year 8 binary number systems quiz">
  <div>
    <h2 class="card-title">Task Title</h2>
    <p class="card-description">One sentence describing what students do.</p>
    <div class="tags">
      <span class="tag">Year 8</span>
      <span class="tag">Binary</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <a href="./Yr8_Binary_Quiz.html" class="btn">Open Task</a>
</div>
```

For an external tool (such as the Python Coding Workspace), use the full URL in `href` and add `target="_blank" rel="noopener"` so it opens in a new tab.

## Please don't

- Put mark schemes, assessments or student data in this repository. It is public.
- Rename or delete another colleague's file without checking with them, as students may already have the link.
